E('pacific ocean', 'The Pacific is the largest and deepest ocean on Earth.', 'Magellan named it in 1520, meaning “peaceful”.', 'It covers about a third of Earth’s surface.', 'It is larger than all the land on Earth combined.', 'The Mariana Trench, its deepest point, is about 11,000 metres deep.', 'The “Ring of Fire” of volcanoes and earthquakes surrounds it.')
E('atlantic ocean', 'The Atlantic is the second-largest ocean.', 'It began opening as Pangaea broke apart around 180 million years ago.', 'It separates the Americas from Europe and Africa.', 'It is still widening by a few centimetres each year.', 'The Gulf Stream carries warm water across it to Europe.')
E('mariana trench|challenger deep', 'The Mariana Trench is the deepest part of the world’s oceans.', 'Its deepest point, the Challenger Deep, was first reached by people in 1960.', 'It lies in the western Pacific.', 'It is about 11,000 metres deep.', 'Jacques Piccard and Don Walsh dived there in the bathyscaphe Trieste.', 'The film director James Cameron dived solo there in 2012.')
E('amazon rainforest|amazon river|the amazon', 'The Amazon is the world’s largest rainforest and one of its greatest rivers.', 'The forest has existed for tens of millions of years.', 'It covers much of South America, mostly in Brazil.', 'It is home to around 10 per cent of all known species.', 'The Amazon River carries more water than any other river.', 'Deforestation threatens large parts of it.')
E('nile|river nile|nile river', 'The Nile is one of the longest rivers in the world.', 'It has supported civilisation in Egypt for over 5,000 years.', 'It flows north about 6,650 kilometres into the Mediterranean.', 'Its two main branches are the White Nile and the Blue Nile.', 'Its yearly flood made Egyptian farming possible.', 'The Aswan High Dam, finished in 1970, now controls the flood.')
E('sahara|sahara desert', 'The Sahara is the largest hot desert in the world.', 'It became a desert around 5,000 years ago; before that it was much greener.', 'It covers much of North Africa.', 'It is almost as large as the United States.', 'Only part of it is sand dunes; much is rock and gravel.', 'Ancient rock art shows giraffes and hippos there.')
E('antarctica continent|antarctic|south pole continent', 'Antarctica is the coldest, windiest and driest continent.', 'It was first sighted in 1820.', 'It is covered by an ice sheet up to about 4.8 kilometres thick.', 'It holds about 70 per cent of the world’s fresh water.', 'The coldest natural temperature on Earth, −89.2 °C, was recorded there in 1983.', 'It has no permanent residents, only researchers.', 'The Antarctic Treaty of 1959 reserves it for peace and science.')
E('pangaea|continental drift|plate tectonics', 'Pangaea was a supercontinent that joined almost all of Earth’s land.', 'It existed about 335 to 175 million years ago.', 'Alfred Wegener proposed continental drift in 1912.', 'Plate tectonics later explained how continents move.', 'The plates move a few centimetres a year.', 'Their movement causes earthquakes, volcanoes and mountains.')
E('continents|seven continents', 'Continents are Earth’s main large landmasses.', 'They formed over hundreds of millions of years of plate movement.', 'They are usually counted as seven: Asia, Africa, North America, South America, Antarctica, Europe and Australia (Oceania).', 'Asia is the largest and most populous.', 'Some traditions count them differently, for example combining the Americas.')
E('south america', 'South America is a continent in the southern part of the Americas.', 'Spain and Portugal colonised most of it from the 16th century.', 'It has 12 independent countries.', 'It contains the Andes, the Amazon and the Atacama, one of the driest deserts on Earth.', 'Spanish and Portuguese are its main languages.')
E('africa', 'Africa is the second-largest continent.', 'It is the birthplace of humanity.', 'It has 54 countries.', 'It has about 1.4 billion people.', 'It is home to the Sahara and the Nile.', 'It has thousands of languages.')
E('asia', 'Asia is the largest and most populous continent.', 'Some of the oldest civilisations began there.', 'It has about 4.7 billion people, around 60 per cent of the world.', 'It contains Mount Everest.', 'It is home to China and India, the two most populous countries.')
E('europe', 'Europe is a continent in the western part of Eurasia.', 'Its history includes ancient Greece and Rome, the Renaissance and the Industrial Revolution.', 'It has around 44 countries.', 'The European Union unites many of them.', 'Its colonial empires once spanned the globe.')
E('mount kilimanjaro|kilimanjaro', 'Mount Kilimanjaro is the highest mountain in Africa.', 'It was first climbed in 1889.', 'It is in Tanzania.', 'It is about 5,895 metres tall.', 'It is a dormant volcano.', 'Its glaciers are shrinking fast.')
E('grand canyon', 'The Grand Canyon is a huge gorge in Arizona.', 'The Colorado River carved it over about 5 to 6 million years.', 'It is about 446 kilometres long.', 'It is up to about 1.8 kilometres deep.', 'Its rocks show nearly two billion years of Earth’s history.')
E('great barrier reef', 'The Great Barrier Reef is the world’s largest coral reef system.', 'Its current form is around 8,000 years old.', 'It lies off north-east Australia.', 'It stretches over 2,300 kilometres.', 'It is home to thousands of species.', 'Warming seas have caused mass coral bleaching.')
E('mediterranean|mediterranean sea', 'The Mediterranean is a sea surrounded by Europe, Africa and Asia.', 'It was the centre of the ancient Western world.', 'Romans called it Mare Nostrum, “our sea”.', 'It connects to the Atlantic through the Strait of Gibraltar.', 'It almost dried up completely about 5.5 million years ago.')
E('volcanoes|volcano|krakatoa', 'Volcanoes are openings in Earth’s crust where molten rock erupts.', 'The 1883 eruption of Krakatoa in Indonesia was one of the deadliest.', 'Krakatoa’s explosion was heard nearly 5,000 kilometres away.', 'The 1815 eruption of Tambora caused a “year without a summer” in 1816.', 'Most volcanoes lie along tectonic plate boundaries.')
E('yellowstone', 'Yellowstone was the world’s first national park.', 'It was established in 1872.', 'It is mostly in Wyoming, in the US.', 'It sits on top of a huge volcanic hotspot.', 'It has the geyser Old Faithful.', 'It is home to bison, wolves and bears.')
E('world population|population of the world|how many people', 'The world’s population is around 8 billion people.', 'It passed 8 billion in November 2022.', 'It was about 1 billion around 1800.', 'It reached 2 billion around 1927.', 'Growth sped up with better medicine and farming.', 'India and China are the most populous countries.')
E('languages|most spoken language|english language', 'There are about 7,000 languages spoken in the world.', 'English developed from Germanic dialects brought to Britain from the 5th century.', 'English and Mandarin Chinese have the most speakers overall.', 'Mandarin has the most native speakers.', 'English took many words from French after 1066 and from Latin.', 'Many languages are endangered.')
E('calendar|gregorian calendar|julian calendar', 'The Gregorian calendar is the calendar used in most of the world.', 'Pope Gregory XIII introduced it in 1582.', 'It replaced the Julian calendar, set up by Julius Caesar.', 'The Julian calendar drifted by about one day every 128 years.', 'Countries switching had to skip days; Britain skipped 11 days in 1752.', 'Russia only switched in 1918.')
